/T (Under U.S. GAAP, tariffs levied on purchases are included in the acquisition cost of inventory. If businesses cannot pass on these cost increases, impairment risks arise. Companies with noncancelable, unhedged commitments may need to recognize expected losses, while supply-chain disruptions may force abnormal overheads to be expensed.)
/E (Under U.S. GAAP, tariffs levied on purchases are included in the acquisition cost of inventory. If businesses cannot pass on these cost increases, impairment risks arise. Companies with noncancelable, unhedged commitments may need to recognize expected losses, while supply-chain disruptions may force abnormal overheads to be expensed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
63 0 obj
