/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 33 0 R
/E (Tariffs may also trigger impairment reviews for long-lived assets and goodwill. Rising costs could render asset groups unrecoverable or require reassessment of fair value. In some cases, entities may abandon assets or accelerate depreciation if supply chains shift or operations become unsustainable. For indefinite-lived intangibles and goodwill, impairment testing may be required when tariffs constitute a triggering event.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
