/Title (Tariffs can significantly affect contract accounting. Increased input costs may alter progress-based revenue recognition \(e.g., cost-to-cost measures\) and create onerous contract losses. Contracts with economic price adjustment clauses may allow tariff-driven increases to be passed to customers as additional revenue. Absent such clauses, changes are recognized only when enforceable as contract modifications.)
